From: Q1000K development <q1000k@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xpon: unwind staged MAC startup and drain owned work

Track completed stages, keep callbacks closed until startup completes, and
propagate failures in workers, QDMA setup, and all WAN netdev creation.
Shutdown timers before freeing state and preserve the dynamic cdev release.
This establishes software cleanup; the legacy QDMA hook is still not a
native Ethernet attachment or a provider lifetime/detach guarantee.

